# WO-04 — Reliable ingestion, bounded health checks, comment counts and program alerts

## Summary

- Findings **R09, R11, R12 and R13 remain OPEN** against current source baseline `9fae324`. This is an English planning document, not implementation or closure evidence.
- Sixteen atomic tasks, seven Evidence Waves, four contract rows, explicit write sets, independent review and QA. No source/test edits, test execution, deployment, data mutation or live messaging today.
- Preserve existing Node22/ESM, Firestore roots, domain identities, authorization and durable delivery semantics. No new dependency by default; no exactly-once FCM claim.
- **Policy gate:** R13 conflicts with the automation contract's fixed Yemen date while the content contract and validator accept per-schedule UTC offsets. Approve the policy/ADR before implementing timezone or receipt changes. Preferred proposal: honor accepted per-schedule offsets with a reviewed compatibility cutover.
- Highest risks: changed RSS identity causing duplicates, stale comment recount overwriting newer counts, and notification key migration resending acknowledged/unknown deliveries. Each has explicit bounded migration/rollback controls.

## Document information

- Date: 2026-10-25. Owner: Delivery Lead. Scope: `hudhud_fm` only.
- Inputs: [technical review](tech-review.md), [content automation](../../docs/contracts/content-automation-contract.md), [station content](../../docs/contracts/station-content-contract.md), [data contract](../../docs/contracts/firebase-data-contract.md), [security](../../docs/contracts/security-privacy-contract.md).
- Existing architecture is retained. No invented PRD or pre-existing new API/module is assumed. All new paths below are marked **PROPOSED NEW**.

