| O-4 | 04-T16 | Separate independent/manual checkpoint; preserve the task prerequisites and evidence |

B01 emits separately reviewed `C01`, `C03`, `C04-RSS`, `C04-HEALTH`, `C04-COUNTS` and `C04-TIMEZONE`. Within B01, I applies01-T01→03-T01→04-T01 shared-contract edits serially. Each downstream batch needs only its named approved output, not full B01 or whole-WO closure. The atomic contract task itself remains incomplete until **all its own outputs** are approved. An unresolved R13 decision blocks `C04-TIMEZONE`/B16 only; it does not block approved unrelated privacy, playback, query, RSS, health or count work.

**B15's shared session removes closure cycles:**04-T06 count work and03-T16 regression scaffolding may proceed on disjoint paths; I applies03-T16 harness scaffolding before04-T08, and04-T07 must precede04-T08. The actual worker integration04-T08 precedes04-T09. Independent01-T14 QA runs after B06 privacy work and the required worker integration. Full03-T16 and01-T14 acceptance are **end-B15 results**, never prerequisites requiring completion before04-T08. All17 previously skipped admin emulator identities must run and pass with the actual worker; corrected-counter controls cannot replace new-comment journeys.

`LOCAL_GREEN` means a scoped contract/source patch is ready for its dependent task. It does **not** mean a spanning runtime wave is `VERIFIED`, the WO is CLOSED, or independent QA/review has passed. In particular `W01-W2` full admin integration and `W03-C` full GREEN wait for B15. The original task dependencies still express data and source prerequisites; same-batch prerequisites are local milestones, not forced agent/WO handoffs. Only the explicit replacements in this addendum change their scheduling interpretation.

Parallel execution additionally requires disjoint writable source paths, approved contracts, distinct available workers, and no shared emulator ports/demo state/harness/config/build output. Shared emulator verification uses one exclusive runtime lock; Flutter/build and web output locks follow the master. Installed Boss runtime argv normalization is not claimed to enforce custom batch/lock metadata automatically; the coordinator checks it before dispatch.

### 4.1 Shared-file ownership and safe parallel work

Only the relevant named approved T01 milestone gates each branch; pending C04-TIMEZONE does not block C04-RSS/HEALTH/COUNTS. RSS T02→T03; health T04→T05; counts T06→T07→T08→T09; notifications T10→T11. T07 waits T05 because both modify `index.js`; T12 waits private schema branches and T08 fixture ownership; T13→T14→T15→T16 closes integration. T03→T09→T11 operational-document edits are serial even when module work is parallel.

After their named approved contract milestones and master batch prerequisites, disjoint module tasks T02, T04, T06 and T10 may run alongside disjoint work in other WOs. T05 cannot run concurrently with T04 because both write stream-health; T07 waits all prior shared index ownership. No overlap is permitted merely because tasks are in different Waves.

**Handoff is not final acceptance:** WO-04 waits only for WO-01/WO-03 approved contract and shared-source-file handoffs, not their full work-order closure. These are INTERIM handoffs with scoped checks; they do not mark an unfinished QA task or Evidence Wave complete. WO-03 final acceptance needs the actual PL03 worker delivered by04-T08, so requiring WO-03 closure before04-T08 would create a forbidden cycle. Likewise, WO-01 integration QA may wait for this worker; WO-01 need not be globally CLOSED before WO-03 starts disjoint authorized work. After integration, rerun the complete required suite—including all17 previously skipped admin emulator checks—before closing affected QA/Waves/findings.

Central integration order: `functions/index.js` **WO-01→WO-03→WO-04**; Rules/tests and shared contracts use the same reviewed handoff order where touched; `firestore.indexes.json` **WO-03→WO-04**, additive only if necessary. `admin-app.tsx`/Excel remain owned by WO-01→WO-03 and are not WO-04 write sets. The emulator harness has one owner, T08; later QA is read-only unless defects return to T08. Rebase and revalidate after each shared handoff.

