## 5. File summary

### 5.1 Proposed new files only

`docs/decisions/0006-background-consistency-and-schedule-timezones.md`; `docs/operations/background-consistency-migrations.md`; `functions/lib/stream-health-progress.js`; `functions/test/stream-health-progress.test.js`; `functions/lib/comment-counts.js`; `functions/test/comment-counts.test.js`; `tool/repair_rss_urls.mjs`; `tool/test/repair_rss_urls.test.mjs`; `tool/reconcile_comment_counts.mjs`; `tool/test/reconcile_comment_counts.test.mjs`; `tool/migrate_program_notification_dates.mjs`; `tool/test/migrate_program_notification_dates.test.mjs`; `firebase_tests/firebase-emulators/editorial-comment-counts.test.js`; `.boss/technical-review/WO-04-validation.md`.

### 5.2 Existing files and serialization

Task write sets are authoritative and contain at most5 paths per task. Shared index T05→T07; health T04→T05; operational document T03→T09→T11→T15→T16; validation T13→T14→T15→T16. Rules/index integration occurs after WO-01/WO-03. Existing `tool/backfill_content_identities.mjs` is a read-only reference unless separately justified and planned; no destructive reuse is assumed.

### 5.3 Verification scope

Node22 Functions unit/lint; existing real emulator scripts and proposed tool tests; tests must identify actual candidate commit and distinguish mocks, emulator worker execution and production evidence. No dependency audit claim, build success, device acceptance, migration execution or production sending is inferred from this plan.

## 6. Standards and closure

Preserve current architecture and error/privacy conventions. Bound queries, retries, scan deadlines and state retention; use transaction reads before writes. Never log raw stream URLs, tokens, account data or comment content. Required QA/reviewer independence is a gate, not self-approval by implementers. Findings remain OPEN until the corresponding fix and authorized operational scope meet their measurable acceptance criteria.

